{"name":"Gypsum","hex":"#eeede4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gypsum","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A mineral consisting of hydrated calcium sulphate. When calcinated, it forms plaster of Paris."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gypsum"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gypsum","blocks":[{"text":"Gypsum is a soft sulfate mineral composed of calcium sulfate dihydrate, with the chemical formula CaSO4·2H2O. It is widely mined and is used as a fertilizer and as the main constituent in many forms of plaster, drywall and blackboard or sidewalk chalk. Gypsum also crystallizes as translucent crystals of selenite. It forms as an evaporite mineral and as a hydration product of anhydrite. The Mohs scale of mineral hardness defines gypsum as hardness value 2 based on scratch hardness comparison."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Gypse_Caresse.jpg/330px-Gypse_Caresse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gypsum","wikidata":"Q82658"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Gypsum_deformed_cristal-MCG_7747-P4150901-black.jpg/500px-Gypsum_deformed_cristal-MCG_7747-P4150901-black.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Gypsum_deformed_cristal-MCG_7747-P4150901-black.jpg/1280px-Gypsum_deformed_cristal-MCG_7747-P4150901-black.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Gypsum_deformed_cristal-MCG_7747-P4150901-black.jpg/500px-Gypsum_deformed_cristal-MCG_7747-P4150901-black.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Gypsum crystals are soft enough to bend under pressure of the hand. Sample on display at Musée cantonal de géologie de Lausanne.","link":"https://en.wiki